   "ordering_read": "THREE-LANE ORDERING RESULT (associational; honest-n carried):\n1. CARE->BOOKINGS (test A): short-lags POSITIVE - t+0 +0.14 (n=30) / t+1 +0.27 (n=26) / t+2 +0.26 (n=19), within-city demeaned per-capita; NYC alone t+0 +0.99 (n=5) - care dollars and arrest-intake co-move in the same window; the negative t+3/t+4 tail (-0.86/-0.87) is thin-n (11/7 pairs, Cincinnati-concentrated).\n2. CARE->MURDERS (test B): NEGATIVE at every lag, pooled deepening -0.16 (t+0) -> -0.42 (t+4, n=15); per-city lane Detroit/Memphis/STL consistently negative through t+1-t+3 - the care-raises-precede-crime-falls ordering signature survives in the component-book panel.\n3. BOOKINGS->MURDERS (test C, mid-stream): raw-lane pooled inverted at t+0/t+1 (-0.46/-0.40, n=51/49) - intake co-moves with violence in-year - while per-city t+3 lane (Boston +0.78 / STL +0.67 / CIN +0.75) hints intake-waves precede later declines, thin-n. The Simes-and-Jahn sharpest-test frame is now data-live but needs facility-grain widening before any mechanism claim.\nNET: the ORDERING the thesis needs is VISIBLE - care co-moves with intake now (A short-lag +) and precedes murder declines (B negative all lags, deepening with lag) - but every strong tail cell is thin-n and the NYC near-perfect cells are trend-artifact-flagged. PATTERN-LEAD, NOT VERDICT (the reproducibility law).",
   "sharpest_next": "facility-grain widening: NYC facility-deep-lane (test D) shows care->admitted t+0 +0.98 (n=7) and the discharges_per_arrest ratio falls 0.18->0.09 across 2015-2024 - the NYC facility book is the only facility-grain city; widening = one more facility-key city (Fulton GA is banked reference-only) or an NYC sub-borough lane."
